     1	"""runtime_paths.py — THE single resolver for per-project runtime state.
     2	
     3	PLAN-182 W1 deliverable. Implements the ADR-001 S318 amendment
     4	(slug becomes normative) + ADR-079 S318 amendment (salt unit = project).
     5	
     6	## Contract (ADR-001 S318 amendment, ratified 2026-08-20)
     7	
     8	1. ``<project-slug>`` is the **native Claude Code path-based slug** of
     9	   the project's absolute path: ``str(path)`` with every ``/`` replaced
    10	   by ``-`` (e.g. ``/Users/<user>/repo`` → ``-Users-<user>-repo``). This is the
    11	   SAME derivation the current harness uses for
    12	   ``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/`` (memory, transcripts), so framework
    13	   runtime state co-locates with harness state for the same project.
    14	2. **One resolver, imported by the whole family.** No file in the
    15	   audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally. Every module
    16	   that previously built the literal
    17	   ``$HOME/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration`` delegates here.
    18	3. **Family-atomicity:** ``runtime_state_dir()`` is the ONE base dir;
    19	   log, key, lock, errors, ``.salt``, rotation siblings and sidecars
    20	   are all resolved as children of it (per-family wrappers may keep
    21	   their own more-specific env overrides, but their DEFAULT is this
    22	   base — never a locally re-derived path).
    23	
    24	## Precedence (highest first)
    25	
    26	1. ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE`` — documented whole-directory override
    27	   (ADR-001 Decision; this module is its FIRST consumer — the original
    28	   spec fiction of an override with zero consumers is repaired here).
    29	2. ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<slug(project_dir())>`` where
    30	   ``project_dir()`` is ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` (the harness-set project
    31	   root) when present, else ``os.getcwd()``.
    32	
    33	## Slug-family archaeology (measured S319, do not "fix")
    34	
    35	``~/.claude/projects/`` holds THREE spellings grown by different
    36	eras/agents:
    37	
    38	- ``--Users-<user>`` (double leading dash): legacy harness derivation
    39	  (``'-' + path.replace('/', '-')``). Frozen legacy trees; never
    40	  written by this module.
    41	- ``-Users-<user>`` (single leading dash): CURRENT harness derivation and
    42	  the ADR-001 normative form. This module emits ONLY this spelling.
    43	- ``ceo-orchestration`` (bare literal): the four-month defect this
    44	  module cures (587-file family, PLAN-182 W0). Reachable read-only via
    45	  :func:`legacy_state_dir` for migration/W2 custody tooling ONLY.
    46	
    47	## Symlink honesty
    48	
    49	``project_dir()`` absolutizes (``os.path.abspath``) but does NOT
    50	``realpath()``: the harness slugs the launch path as given, and native
    51	alignment (co-location with harness memory) wins over symlink
    52	canonicalization. Two spellings of one repo via symlinks therefore get
    53	two state dirs — same behavior the harness itself has for its memory
    54	dirs. Documented limitation, pinned by test.
    55	
    56	## CLI contract (PLAN-182 OQ-6 — Owner decision 2026-08-22, landed S326)
    57	
    58	Shell consumers get the SAME resolver, never a rebuilt literal::
    59	
    60	    python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py [--state-dir | --slug |
    61	                                                 --project-dir] [--project PATH]
    62	
    63	- ``--state-dir`` (default): :func:`runtime_state_dir`; ``--slug``:
    64	  :func:`project_slug`; ``--project-dir``: the slug input.
    65	- ``--project PATH`` replaces the slug INPUT (``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` / cwd).
    66	  ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE`` still wins for ``--state-dir`` — it is the
    67	  documented operator override, not a default.
    68	- Read-only: prints ONE path + newline on stdout, creates nothing, exit 0.
    69	  Usage error: exit 2, message on stderr, NOTHING on stdout (a caller doing
    70	  ``dir="$(...)"`` must never capture prose as a path).
    71	- ONE invocation convention. An inline ``python3 -c`` in a template would
    72	  be a second one, and the class this cures is "a local branch that
    73	  re-derives the path" (CLAUDE.md §4). Consumers: the two pre-push review
    74	  gates in ``templates/{codex,grok}/``, ``ceo-backup.sh``, ``ceo-restore.sh``.
    75	
    76	Leaf module: stdlib only, imports nothing from ``_lib`` (loadable from
    77	any hook, mirrors ``injection_salt``'s constraint). Python ≥ 3.9.
    78	"""
    79	
    80	from __future__ import annotations
    81	
    82	import os
    83	import stat as stat_mod
    84	import sys
    85	from pathlib import Path
    86	from typing import List, Optional, Union
